Ladybird shapes each run of text on a path in the style of the element
the run is in. For a <tspan> with a font-size of its own inside a
<textPath>, getComputedTextLength() and getSubStringLength() return the
same lengths in Chrome 157.0.8103.79, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5
as in Ladybird. Blink lays text on a path in SvgTextLayoutAlgorithm::
PositionOnPath(), WebKit in SVGTextLayoutAlgorithm::positionOnPaths(),
and Gecko in SVGTextFrame::DoTextPathLayout() — each from glyphs that
were shaped per element. Gecko’s bounding box for the text is 2px wider
on each side than that of Blink, WebKit, and Ladybird.
